# Special relativity 32 — The relativistic Kepler problem: Sommerfeld's rosette
#
# (Goldstein 3rd ed., §7.10 and Exercise 7.27; Jackson 3rd ed., Problem 12.4 (a similar setup);
#  Sommerfeld, Ann. Phys. 51, 1 (1916); Landau & Lifshitz, Classical Theory of
#  Fields, §39 and Problem 39.1.)
# A (classical, spinless) electron moves in the Coulomb field of a gold nucleus,
# Z = 79, with the relativistic equations of motion
#     r' = p c² / E_kin,   p' = −k r / |r|³,   E_kin = √(p² c² + m² c⁴),  k = Z e²/(4π ε₀).
# It starts at a turning point r₀ = 3 ħ/(m c) on the x axis with momentum p₀ = 0.500 m c
# along y, so its angular momentum is L = r₀ p₀ = 1.5 ħ.
#   (a) The total energy E = E_kin − k/r, and check it is bound (E < m c²).
#   (b) The orbit does not close: each radial period the turning point advances by
#         Δφ = 2π (1/√(1 − (k/(L c))²) − 1)     (Landau & Lifshitz §39),
#       i.e. by 2π(1/√(1 − (Zα/1.5)²) − 1). Integrate for a few radial periods, find the
#       times of the next two turning points of the same kind (where r · p changes sign
#       the same way), and measure the advance of the turning-point angle.
#   (c) The radial period from the ODE against T_r = ∮ dr / ṙ by quadrature:
#       T_r = 2 ∫ E_kin(r) dr / (c² p_r(r)) from r_min to r_max, with E_kin = E + k/r and
#       p_r² = ((E + k/r)² − m²c⁴)/c² − L²/r²; r₀ turns out to be r_min.

Z = 79
k = Z e² / (4π ε_0)
r0 = 3 ħ / (m_e c)
p0 = 0.500 m_e c
L = r0 p0
Ekin(p) = √(|p|² c² + m_e² c⁴)
E = √(p0² c² + m_e² c⁴) - k / r0
print "(a) L/hbar =", L / ħ to 8 digits, " Z alpha =", k / (ħ c) to 8 digits, " E/(m c²) =", E / (m_e c²) to 10 digits, " bound:", E < m_e c²

solve r' = p c² / Ekin(p),
      p' = -k r / |r|^3
  with r(0 s) = <r0, 0 m>, p(0 s) = <0 kg m/s, p0>
  for t from 0 s to 3e-19 s tolerance 1e-12

# turning points: r · p crosses zero. At t = 0 the electron is at the far point
# (apocentre) or the near one; find every crossing of the same sign as the first
radial(t) = r(t) · p(t)
n_scan = 30000
dt = 3e-19 s / n_scan
tps = []
for i from 2 to n_scan
    a = radial((i - 1) dt)
    b = radial(i dt)
    if a > 0 kg m²/s and b <= 0 kg m²/s
        solve radial(tc) = 0 kg m²/s for tc from (i - 1) dt to i dt
        push(tps, tc)
angle(t) = atan2(r(t).y, r(t).x)
T_r = tps[2] - tps[1]
adv = angle(tps[2]) - angle(tps[1])
adv = if adv < 0 then adv + 2π else adv
print "(b) turning points found:", len(tps), " advance per radial period =", adv in ° to 8 digits
print "    Sommerfeld 2π(1/√(1 − (k/Lc)²) − 1) =", 2π (1 / √(1 - (k / (L c))²) - 1) in ° to 8 digits
print "    first turning angle =", angle(tps[1]) in ° to 8 digits, " |r| there =", |r(tps[1])| / r0 to 8 digits

# (c) the radial period by quadrature between the turning points r_min, r_max
pr2(x) = ((E + k / x)² - m_e² c⁴) / c² - L² / x²
solve pr2(rmax) = 0 kg² m²/s² for rmax from 1.01 r0 to 20 r0
print "(c) r_max/r0 =", rmax / r0 to 10 digits, " T_r (ODE) =", T_r to 9 digits
T_q = 2 ∫ (E + k / x) / (c² √(pr2(x))) dx from r0 to rmax
print "    T_r (quadrature) =", T_q to 9 digits
